{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q412589","formula":"C₁₀H₁₉NO","hill":"C10H19NO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":19.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Lupinine","ru":"Люпинин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Lupinine is a quinolizidine alkaloid present in the genus Lupinus (colloquially referred to as lupins) of the flowering plant family Fabaceae. The scientific literature contains many reports on the isolation and synthesis of this compound as well as a vast number of studies on its biosynthesis from its natural precursor, lysine. Studies have shown that lupinine hydrochloride is a mildly toxic acetylcholinesterase inhibitor and that lupinine has an inhibitory effect on acetylcholine receptors.","ru":"Люпинин — алкалоид, содержащийся в некоторых видах люпина. Наиболее богаты им семена. Легко растворим в воде, спирте, хлороформе, эфире."},"fame":15,"pubchemCid":91461,"mass":169.26,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CCN2CCC[C@H]([C@H]2C1)CO","inchikey":"HDVAWXXJVMJBAR-VHSXEESVSA-N","iupac":"[(1R,9aR)-2,3,4,6,7,8,9,9a-octahydro-1H-quinolizin-1-yl]methanol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"91461","atoms":31,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.1,"y":-1.499,"z":0.599,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.673,"y":0.801,"z":0.344,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.285,"y":-0.267,"z":-0.606,"el":"C"},{"x":1.244,"y":-0.547,"z":-0.565,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.094,"y":-1.554,"z":-0.351,"el":"C"},{"x":2.017,"y":0.754,"z":-0.825,"el":"C"},{"x":0.06,"y":2.051,"z":0.075,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.121,"y":1.073,"z":0.296,"el":"C"},{"x":1.574,"y":1.861,"z":0.124,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.594,"y":-1.293,"z":-0.398,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.954,"y":-0.176,"z":0.571,"el":"C"},{"x":1.725,"y":-1.205,"z":0.736,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.525,"y":0.073,"z":-1.625,"el":"H"},{"x":1.49,"y":-1.231,"z":-1.39,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.864,"y":-1.974,"z":0.635,"el":"H